{"title":"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The bar graph below shows the numbers of boys and girls in Mrs. Kuwabara’s class. The percentage of students in the class who are girls is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a8ceb1bdf666007c7fb7010c7fd5cb083caa89a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 40\\% \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 15\\% \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 25\\% \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 10\\% \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"472\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can first find the the number of girls in the class and the total number of students.\n</p><p>From the bar graph, we can see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> girls and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> boys. This means that the total number of students is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5593cdcced3b1eaa4cb3b678f48ea19912180b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 15 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We can then see that the percentage of girls in the class is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9707e988e71177feaa6a446ca1c840a143a5b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{25} \\times 100\\% = 0.4 \\times 100\\% = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 40\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"305\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a 